Restructures input handling to separate hardware layer (managers) from gameplay logic (ECS system), adds synchronous Pull API alongside event-based Push API, and optimizes entity iteration with caching.

Core Changes

Pull API for Input State Queries

KeyboardManager: BeginFrame(), IsKeyHeld(), IsKeyPressed(), IsKeyReleased() with per-frame edge detection
JoystickManager: GetButton(), IsButtonPressed(), IsButtonReleased(), GetAxis() with JoystickState tracking
Frame state reset in main loop before event processing

InputMappingSystem (New ECS System)

Reads manager state via Pull API, maps hardware input to gameplay actions. Replaces direct keyboard→component mutation in EventManager.

// Before: EventManager directly mutates PlayerController_data from keyboard events
// After: InputMappingSystem polls KeyboardManager each frame
void InputMappingSystem::Process() {
    if (InputsManager::Get().GetActiveContext() != InputContext::Gameplay) return;

