Controller_data Restructure

Separate leftStick/rightStick vectors, leftTrigger/rightTrigger floats
Button array reduced to MAX_BUTTONS=16 constant (shared with JoystickManager)
Axes properly mapped: 0→leftStick.x, 1→leftStick.y, 2→rightStick.x, etc.

InputMapping_data Component

Rebindable key/button mappings per entity with deadzone/sensitivity:

struct InputMapping_data {
    std::unordered_map<std::string, SDL_Scancode> keyboardBindings;
    std::unordered_map<std::string, int> gamepadBindings;
    float deadzone = 0.15f;
    void InitializeDefaults();  // WASD + Arrows
};

Input Context Stack

PushContext(UI) / PopContext() controls whether InputMappingSystem processes input. Enables menu overlays without gameplay interference.

Entity Cache Optimization

InputsManager maintains m_inputEntities vector
Auto-populated when AddComponent<PlayerBinding_data>() via template specialization
EventManager_ECS uses cache (~10 entities) vs full entity map iteration (~1000s)

Main Loop Order

BeginFrame()           // Reset per-frame input state
→ SDL_PollEvent()      // Platform events → managers
→ EventManager::Process()  // Dispatch queued messages
→ World::Process()     // InputMappingSystem runs here
→ Render()

Constants & Cleanup

Controller_data::MAX_BUTTONS, JoystickManager::MAX_AXES replace magic numbers
French comments translated to English
MouseManager::BeginFrame() stub for API consistency
