Implements Alt+ key combinations for menu access from anywhere in the console application. Alt+E in screens focuses the first editable field instead of opening the Edit menu.

## Changes

**Console Application (EbsApp.java)**
- Scene-level event filter captures Alt+F/E/C/T/S/H globally
- Menu lookup by text name rather than index for resilience to menu reordering
- Maps: File, Edit, Config, Tools, Screens, Help menus respectively

**Screens (ScreenFactory.java)**
- Alt+E handler searches bound controls for first focusable editable field
- Supports TextField, TextArea, ComboBox, ChoiceBox, DatePicker, ColorPicker, Spinner, ScriptArea

## Implementation

```java
// Console: Global menu access
scene.addEventFilter(KeyEvent.KEY_PRESSED, event -> {
    if (!event.isAltDown() || event.isControlDown() || event.isShiftDown()) return;

    if (event.getCode() == KeyCode.F) showMenuByName("File");
    else if (event.getCode() == KeyCode.E) showMenuByName("Edit");
    // ... other menu mappings
});

// Screens: Focus first editor
else if (event.getCode() == KeyCode.E && event.isAltDown() 
         && !event.isControlDown() && !event.isShiftDown()) {
    focusFirstEditableField(allBoundControls);
}
```

Context-dependent behavior: Alt+E opens Edit menu in console, focuses editor in screens.

